13850	{"artifactId":"LLD-c32aa60534232f36-s5","entry":{"id":"review-5e5b29679f181ea46de4e181ad92006b","actor":{"id":"insrc:review","kind":"system","properties":{}},"timestamp":"2026-10-29T10:36:21.961Z","operation":"review","outcome":{"result":"warn","summary":"review: warn","data":{"kind":"review","report":{"artifact":"design.story","stage":"design.story","verdict":"warn","findings":[{"claimId":"coverage-of-intent.1","ref":"coverage-of-intent","item":"coverage-of-intent","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"The LLD's acceptance-mapping table (§7) covers exactly s5's DEF acceptance criteria ac1-ac4 (completeness guard, adjudication, publication fault matrix, post-review freshness), with no invented criteria and no non-goal built beyond those.","evidence":"DEF.md §6.5 (lines 155-168) lists s5 ac1-ac4 with text matching the LLD's acceptance-mapping rows verbatim in intent (completion guard / adjudication / publication fault matrix / post-review freshness). The LLD's §7 'Acceptance mapping' table maps tests to exactly ac1-ac4, and §3's new/changed files (completion-types, completion-assessment, completion-publication, completion-artifact, completion-publisher) all serve those four criteria without adding unrelated capability. [files: docs/epics/review-planned-changes-through-agent-investigation-E20261028c32aa605/DEF.md]","action":"Read DEF.md story s5 section and cross-checked against LLD §7 acceptance table.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"coverage-of-intent.2","ref":"coverage-of-intent","item":"coverage-of-intent","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"The LLD does not implement work reserved to oq1 (the sc4 prerequisite) as part of s5's own build scope; it is explicitly deferred to an amendment.","evidence":"§3.5 states 'sc5 consumes that capability and must not implement sc4 reducer/lease changes as its own task' and names a 'Formal pending proposal: .insrc/artifacts/AMD-c32aa60534232f36-1.json. This is a prerequisite amendment request, not an implemented capability.' The AMD file itself is a draft amendment (lifecycle.status:'draft') proposing a sharedContract.methodAdd on sc4, not a change folded into s5's own task list. [files: .insrc/artifacts/AMD-c32aa60534232f36-1.json]","action":"Read AMD-c32aa60534232f36-1.json.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"current-behaviour.1","ref":"current-behaviour","item":"current-behaviour","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"The current sc4 (RecoveryStore.claim) implementation rejects a new lease claim once the run is in the 'completion-requested' state, as the LLD §3.5 claims ('The current sc4 implementation rejects lease claims for completion-requested state').","evidence":"recovery-lifecycle.ts:21 — if(['completed','cancelled','stale','completion-requested'].includes(old.state))throw new RecoveryError('corrupt','Cannot claim terminal/completion run.'); inside the lease event branch, which is the only path RecoveryStore.claim() (recovery-store.ts:43-47) drives. [files: src/workflow/code-review/investigation/recovery-lifecycle.ts, src/workflow/code-review/investigation/recovery-store.ts]","action":"Read recovery-lifecycle.ts and recovery-store.ts.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"current-behaviour.2","ref":"current-behaviour","item":"current-behaviour","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"sc4's current ReviewRecoveryV1/RecoveryStore has no accepted publication-intent binding field or operation (no 'intentRef' concept), matching the LLD's claim that this capability is missing today.","evidence":"HLD.md §5.4's ReviewRecoveryV1 interface sketch (lines 243-258) carries only completionReceipt: string | null, no intent field. recovery-store.ts's public surface (claim/renew/release/requestCompletion/recordCompletion/issueAttempt/settleAttempt/extendAllowance/recordUsage) has no intent-staging method; recordCompletion takes only a receipt: string, confirming no durable intent binding exists. [files: docs/epics/review-planned-changes-through-agent-investigation-E20261028c32aa605/HLD.md, src/workflow/code-review/investigation/recovery-store.ts]","action":"Read HLD.md §5.4 and recovery-store.ts in full.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"current-behaviour.3","ref":"current-behaviour","item":"current-behaviour","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"CodeReviewBody.groundingMode is currently a closed union of exactly 'full' | 'degraded' with no 'investigation' member, matching §3.3's premise that this is a genuine extension, not something already present.","evidence":"src/workflow/code-review/types.ts:133 and :234 both declare readonly groundingMode: 'full' | 'degraded'; with no third variant; runner.ts's RunCodeReviewOpts.groundingMode and buildArtifact mirror the same two-value union. [files: src/workflow/code-review/types.ts, src/workflow/code-review/runner.ts]","action":"Grepped and read src/workflow/code-review/types.ts and runner.ts.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"new-versus-reuse.1","ref":"new-versus-reuse","item":"new-versus-reuse","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"The severity fold the LLD says it 'preserves exactly' (any HIGH block, else MED warn, else pass) is the fold actually implemented today in the runner the design reuses.","evidence":"runner.ts foldVerdict (lines 303-313): counts.high > 0 ? 'block' : counts.med > 0 ? 'warn' : 'pass', with the warn-cap only ever raising a 'pass' to 'warn', never lowering block/warn — exactly as §3.3 describes ('Preserve current severity fold exactly... confidence remains explicit'). [files: src/workflow/code-review/runner.ts]","action":"Read runner.ts foldVerdict/validateArtifact.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"new-versus-reuse.2","ref":"new-versus-reuse","item":"new-versus-reuse","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"ArtifactStore.updateAndLog, which §3.4's publisher claims to reuse for a guarded compare-current-head-then-mutate canonical write, exists with that exact compare/mutate shape.","evidence":"artifact-core/store.ts:188-203 — updateAndLog reads the current head (await this.read(id)) plus its change log, passes it to a caller-supplied mutate that returns undefined (no-op) or {next, options}, and only then calls writeUnlocked. This matches the LLD's claim of an existing guarded content-mutation primitive to build the expected-revision CAS on, rather than a new storage primitive. [files: src/workflow/artifact-core/store.ts]","action":"Read artifact-core/store.ts.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"new-versus-reuse.3","ref":"new-versus-reuse","item":"new-versus-reuse","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"The proposed sc5 files (completion-types.ts, completion-assessment.ts, completion-publication.ts, completion-artifact.ts, completion-publisher.ts) do not already exist, so labelling them 'new' is accurate.","evidence":"Glob of src/workflow/code-review/investigation/*.ts lists 27 existing files (types, identity, subject, work, ledger*, progress, navigation, continuation*, recovery-*, git-packets, source, index) — none named completion-types / completion-assessment / completion-publication / completion-artifact / completion-publisher. [files: src/workflow/code-review/investigation/]","action":"Glob the investigation/ directory.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"change-sites.1","ref":"change-sites","item":"change-sites","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"party.ts's authorPartyOf has the exact fallback behavior (explicit authoredBy wins, else per-output 'client'/other label, else 'unknown') that §3.1 relies on for its 'same author/reviewer' conflict check ('re-read canonical BUILD authorPartyOf and authenticated review party, not model-supplied labels').","evidence":"party.ts:42-53 authorPartyOf implements exactly that precedence, and reviewerPartyOf (lines 64-72) mirrors it for the review side, giving s5 a real, already-shipped function to call rather than a function it must invent. [files: src/workflow/review/party.ts]","action":"Read party.ts in full.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"change-sites.2","ref":"change-sites","item":"change-sites","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"The listed call sites for the new/changed artifacts (ledger.ts, recovery-store.ts, types.ts, runner.ts, artifact-core/store.ts) are the actual files that own the capabilities the design says they consume (ledger validation, sc4 recovery, CodeReviewBody/Artifact types, the runner, the artifact store), not files invented or mis-attributed.","evidence":"Confirmed by direct reads/greps: recovery-store.ts owns RecoveryStore.requestCompletion/recordCompletion exactly as cited in §2.3; types.ts owns CodeReviewBody.groundingMode as cited in §3.3; runner.ts owns buildArtifact/foldVerdict as cited in §3.3/3.4; artifact-core/store.ts owns updateAndLog as cited in §3.4. [files: src/workflow/code-review/investigation/recovery-store.ts, src/workflow/code-review/types.ts, src/workflow/code-review/runner.ts, src/workflow/artifact-core/store.ts]","action":"Cross-checked each cited call site against its file contents.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"data-compatibility.1","ref":"data-compatibility","item":"data-compatibility","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"The LLD's claim that 'old [CR] records omit [body.investigation] and remain readable' is a realistic backward-compat design, and its companion claim that 'enum-strict older readers... are NOT automatically compatible' correctly flags a real present-day risk around the groundingMode extension.","evidence":"The LLD's own proposed type snippet declares investigation?: {...} | undefined as optional, consistent with additive backward compatibility. But I found no existing runtime reader/validator in the codebase (no file matching completion-evidence*, no exhaustive switch over groundingMode in gate.ts) that already enforces or would break on an unrecognized groundingMode value, so I cannot confirm whether the characterization of enum-strict readers as a real risk is accurate versus overstated — the actual readers that would need s6 capability-gating are not yet identified in code. [files: src/workflow/code-review/gate.ts]","action":"Grepped for 'completion-evidence' files (none found) and for exhaustive groundingMode switches in gate.ts (none found); grepped 35 files referencing groundingMode across daemon/mcp/workflow layers without exhaustively auditing each for strict-enum behavior.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"could-not-verify"},{"claimId":"boundaries.1","ref":"boundaries","item":"boundaries","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"s5's design does not implement sc4's internal lease/journal/reducer logic itself; the one new sc4 capability it needs (withPublicationFence) is routed through the formal amendment mechanism (AMD artifact) rather than coded directly inside an s5-owned file.","evidence":"The AMD-c32aa60534232f36-1.json body carries amendment.type:'sharedContract.methodAdd', contractId:'sc4' and is attributed to proposedBy: {workflow:'design.story', storyId:'s5', stepId:'s4'} — i.e. it is a typed cross-story proposal, exactly the mechanism described for downstream Stories proposing HLD/contract changes, and the LLD's own §3.5 explicitly disclaims private sc4 implementation by s5 ('sc5 consumes that capability and must not implement sc4 reducer/lease changes as its own task'). [files: .insrc/artifacts/AMD-c32aa60534232f36-1.json]","action":"Read the AMD artifact and cross-checked its proposedBy/type fields against the amendment mechanism and against LLD §3.5's own wording.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"error-paths.1","ref":"error-paths","item":"error-paths","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"The RecoveryError codes the LLD's Contract-details section cites for RecoveryStore ('Corrupt, unsupported or foreign recovery state; ownership lost') are the actual codes the type defines, so the error taxonomy in §2.3/§6 is not inventing error kinds that don't exist in the reused sc4 surface.","evidence":"recovery-types.ts:20 declares export type RecoveryErrorCode = 'invalid-input' | 'corrupt' | 'unsupported' | 'stale' | 'ownership-lost' ... and recovery-store.ts/recovery-lifecycle.ts throw exactly these codes (corrupt for lifecycle violations, ownership-lost for stale leases, invalid-input for malformed input) — matching the LLD's error-path language. [files: src/workflow/code-review/investigation/recovery-types.ts, src/workflow/code-review/investigation/recovery-store.ts, src/workflow/code-review/investigation/recovery-lifecycle.ts]","action":"Read recovery-types.ts and cross-checked thrown codes in recovery-store.ts / recovery-lifecycle.ts.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"tests.1","ref":"tests","item":"tests","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"Every s5 DEF acceptance criterion (ac1-ac4) is mapped to at least one named planned test in the LLD's §7 acceptance-mapping table, so no acceptance criterion is left without a test obligation.","evidence":"LLD §7 'Acceptance mapping' table has one row each for ac1, ac2, ac3, ac4, each naming at least one 'Proving tests' entry (e.g. ac1 → 'Each missing/pending/unverified ... row or unfinished block returns incomplete with no canonical write.' and a second test; ac3 → three distinct proving tests covering the crash/concurrency/mode-parity matrix).","action":"Read LLD §7 acceptance-mapping table directly.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"}],"counts":{"high":0,"med":0,"low":14,"unverified":1},"template":"design-spec","reviewedAt":"2026-10-29T10:36:21.961Z","model":"cli-claude:claude-sonnet-5","reviewedBy":"daemon"},"resolutions":{}}}}}
